{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nF12 verification on commit 8a036765705f5ef0e7db4fa21e0926e51d15bafd exposed a long-running `test_resign_routes_through_pin_collecting_sign_path`. An isolated run on current `origin/main` commit 51621917bfc635d7673cb0519a400afda12eb2cb reproduced the delay. The test body reported PASS after 201.81 seconds. The process exited after 524.52 seconds. Pytest attributed 5.15 seconds to setup and 0.06 seconds to teardown. A one-second process sample during the remaining post-PASS interval showed recursive filesystem deletion dominated by `unlinkat` and `rmdir`.\n\nClosed tickets `grindable-deviant-angwantibo` and `asbestos-popular-tench` repaired omitted private `--basetemp` arguments in nested pytest children. This reproduction occurs in an ordinary test session and needs separate lifecycle tracing. Active ticket `famished-disgustful-gypsymoth` changes timeout coverage for fixture phases. Active ticket `expectable-slowwitted-squeaker` covers a local Git child timeout. Neither ticket records this test or its post-PASS deletion interval.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce the delay in an isolated current-main worktree and capture phase timings, the active temporary path, file counts, allocated bytes, and a Python stack during the post-PASS interval.\n- Trace the fixture and pytest lifecycle that creates and removes the snapshot tree.\n- Distinguish test-call snapshot materialization cost, session-finish cleanup cost, shared temporary-root cleanup, and host filesystem contention with discriminating experiments.\n- Determine whether pending Gerrit change 2141 guards the affected phase or only changes the terminal failure mode.\n- Establish the intended behavior from the maintained timeout and test-runtime policy.\n- Confirm the root cause and defect origin before proposing any repair.\n- If a repair is warranted, update this ticket with the fix plan and file impact, obtain a current plan review, and prove the repair with a RED-first held-out oracle.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A current-main reproduction records call time, total time, and the post-PASS stack.\n- [x] Runtime evidence identifies the lifecycle phase and the changeable artifact responsible for the delay.\n- [x] Discriminating experiments reject the surviving alternative explanations.\n- [x] The relationship to `grindable-deviant-angwantibo`, `asbestos-popular-tench`, `famished-disgustful-gypsymoth`, and `expectable-slowwitted-squeaker` is recorded.\n- [x] The defect origin is proven or the RCA records the completed unattributable search.\n- [x] The RCA is recorded before any repair begins.\n- [x] Any repair uses a RED-first oracle, preserves unrelated test behavior, and passes its declared verification."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787555419663075001,"uuid":"f99d7d3a-67fb-4066-a767-36b82d089abe"}